@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam ArrowFontStyle plain
skinparam sequenceParticipantFontColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

participant ":MainWindow" as UI UI_COLOR
participant ":LogicManager" as Logic LOGIC_COLOR
participant "mark:MarkCommand" as Mark LOGIC_COLOR
participant "candidate:ModelManager" as Candidate MODEL_COLOR
participant ":StorageManager" as Storage STORAGE_COLOR
participant "live:ModelManager" as Live MODEL_COLOR

UI -> Logic : execute("mark 2 1 2 m/CS2103T w/1 s/present")
activate UI
activate Logic
note over Logic, Mark
Parsing and command creation omitted.
MarkCommand deduplicates indices to [2, 1].
Scenario assumes valid input and enrolment.
end note
note over Logic
executeStudentReplacement(mark) snapshots
the full original roster and displayed rows.
end note
create Candidate
Logic -> Candidate : new ModelManager(...)
activate Candidate
Candidate --> Logic
deactivate Candidate
Logic -> Candidate : updateFilteredPersonList(displayed::contains)
activate Candidate
Candidate --> Logic
deactivate Candidate
Logic -> Mark : execute(candidate)
activate Mark
note over Mark, Candidate
getTargets(candidate) resolves one displayed snapshot.
Check ALL bounds, then ALL enrolments in input order.
Build replacements with Person.withAttendance(decision).
Keep original objects for unchanged decisions.
Detailed accessors and Person calls are omitted.
end note
loop each changed target
Mark -> Candidate : setPerson(target, updated)
activate Candidate
Candidate --> Mark
deactivate Candidate
end
Mark --> Logic : result (counts; first unique target selected)
deactivate Mark
note over Logic, Candidate
Compare complete proposed and original rosters.
The selected student alone may be unchanged.
end note

alt proposed.equals(original)
Logic --> UI : result (Attendance unchanged)
note over UI, Logic
Select first target; clear input; retain context.
No disk write or live replacement for an unchanged batch.
end note
else at least one row differs
alt save succeeds
Logic -> Storage : saveAddressBook(candidate.getAddressBook())
activate Storage
Storage --> Logic : return
deactivate Storage
loop each changed row, in original roster order
Logic -> Live : setPerson(original.get(i), proposed.get(i))
activate Live
Live --> Logic
deactivate Live
end
Logic --> UI : result (Attendance set)
note over UI
Select first target; refresh details; clear input.
Retain class/week context and row order.
end note
else save fails
Logic -> Storage : saveAddressBook(candidate.getAddressBook())
activate Storage
Storage --> Logic : IOException
deactivate Storage
note over Logic
Log failure; wrap in CommandException.
end note
Logic --> UI : CommandException
note over UI, Live
Show error; retain input, selection, details, badges, heading and data.
No live.setPerson call for ANY target and no success result on this path.
end note
end
end

deactivate Logic
deactivate UI
@enduml
